## What I built

`apps/qcraft-web` — Vite + React 18 + TS + D3 static app, 8 commits on `feat/lane2-ui`, following the `debt-projection-tool-v2` conventions I studied first.

All five tabs (Baseline, Analysis, Climate, Data, Methodology), the sidebar with the five newly exposed parameters (productivity start/long-run, inflation start/end, interest-rate approach) defaulting to the engine's own `DEFAULTS`, guidance tooltips sourced per-entry, and a theme copied verbatim from the brand tokens (reachable; font names only, no files).

## Three things worth your attention

**The build is mock-backed, and the app says so.** `SHARED/engine-api.md` landed mid-session at 12:44, but the engine package lives in lane 1's clone, so `@qcraft/engine` isn't importable from here. I coded the seam against the contract anyway and wrote + tested the `PipelineResult → EngineResult` mapping, so the swap is an import plus one line. The in-app banner lists every parameter you changed that the backend couldn't honour, and it's driven by provenance, so it self-removes.

**I got the scenario colours wrong, then the contract corrected me.** The engine's `COLORS` dict genuinely fails a measurement — Hot+Unadapted vs High sit at normal-vision ΔE 9.0 against a floor of 15, and those are the two lines the Analysis tab exists to compare. My first replacement was a single warming ramp. §7 of the contract rules that out, and it's right: `High` (67.8) ends below `Hot` (94.0) because they're different NGFS pathways, so a ramp asserts a ladder the data doesn't have. I'd noticed the anomaly, documented it, and encoded it anyway. Now it's three hues for the standalone pathways plus one hue in three steps for the 3°C family. This is open question 3 — if the Uganda slides already show the old colours, continuity may outweigh separation, and that's your call.

**Rendering it caught three defects that build, lint, and tests all passed.** The Climate tab's lead chart stated a damage number it was physically unable to show (GDP grows tenfold; a 6% shortfall is a line width), a peak annotation collided with the WEO label, and GDP axis ticks truncated to ",000,000". Fixed, and `scripts/screenshot.mjs` is there so the Saturday freeze can re-run the pass.

One repair outside my lane: the root `pyproject.toml` globs `apps/*`, so my npm directory broke every `uv run` in the repo. Excluded it — `198 passed` confirms the Python lane is intact.

Verification: build ✓, lint 0 problems, 26/26 vitest (35 golden-master rows matched to 9 dp), 198/198 pytest, all 5 tabs render with no console errors. Details and the four open questions are in `MORNING-REPORT.md`.
